cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this model or its results, please cite it as below."
type: software

title: "Wildfire Smoke Shelter Placement Agent-Based Model"
abstract: >-
  An agent-based model of clean-air shelter access for unsheltered residents
  of Multnomah County, Oregon during a wildfire smoke episode. 6,842 residents
  with individually sampled age, sex, mobility, asthma and COPD attributes
  start at real reported campsite locations and walk Portland's real street
  network toward the nearest shelter with room, driven by measured hourly
  PM2.5 from the September 2020 smoke event. Three scenarios separate the
  effect of total shelter capacity from the effect of how that capacity is
  split across sites, with a triage arm testing bed reserves for
  mobility-limited residents.

